<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed stronger at 3.29 pct below parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed stronger at 3.29 pct below parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.4850 to the dollar, up from 3.4990 on Thursday and at 1.9360 to the mark, up from 1.9490, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of 3.29 percent below the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, stronger than Thursday's fix at -3.91 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
